    "result_text": "The build is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `initials` field on the owner response.\n\n**Change 1 \u2014 `src/main/resources/openapi.yml`**: Added an `initials` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema (alongside the existing `displayName`), so the generated `OwnerDto` gains a corresponding field.\n\n**Change 2 \u2014 `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`**: Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` that computes `initials` as the upper-cased first letters of `firstName` and `lastName`, dot-separated with a trailing dot (e.g. `john`/`smith` \u2192 `J.S.`).\n\nThe mapping flows through the existing `RespondWithOwner` OfficeFloor function, which serializes `OwnerDto`, so `GET /api/owners/{id}` now returns `initials`.\n\nTests: `AcceptanceTest.coreComputesInitials` passes, and the full suite is `BUILD SUCCESS` (1 test, 0 failures).",
